# Monitor cursor-rules sync

This workspace **hard-links** monitor cursor rules between:

| Tree | Role |
|------|------|
| **`.cursor/rules/`** | Active for Cursor in this workspace |
| **`HPCPerfStats/monitor/cursor-rules/`** | Shipped with the monitor package / full-stack checkout |

In **this** checkout, editing either path updates the same inode. In other checkouts they may be separate copies — then you must update **both** trees in one commit.

## When creating or editing rules

1. Use the same filename in both trees (or rely on hard-links here).
2. After editing, `diff .cursor/rules/<f> HPCPerfStats/monitor/cursor-rules/<f>` in unfamiliar checkouts.
3. New monitor-themed rules belong in **both** locations unless workspace-only meta rules.

## Related rules index

After adding a rule, add a one-line cross-link in **implementation-workflow-discipline.mdc** (Related rules table) when agents should consult it during implement/verify.

Cross-links: **cursor-rules-maker**, **chat-analysis-for-rules**.
